# Anonymized excerpt modelled on a full-size Player.log, for the log
# parser's unit tests. Every mod-derived name, def and path below is
# invented (the Ludeon ids are the real vanilla ones); the line shapes are
# the real ones. The '#' lines are this file's own annotations and match
# no log shape.
#
# Deliberate properties this fixture tests:
#  - 7 terse '... failed' lines but only 4 stack-trace blocks. The real log
#    pairs them 1:1; an excerpt does not, so the parser must tolerate a
#    terse failure with no block, and a block with no terse line, rather
#    than assuming the pairing holds.
#  - Line endings: the real log is CRLF and contains 3 lone \r characters.
#    Rust's str::lines() splits on \n and strips one trailing \r, which
#    matches grep and sed. Python's splitlines() does not - it splits the
#    lone \r as well, shifting every line number after it by one. Split
#    on \n, never on "any line break".
#
# header: engine banner, then the RimWorld version this log came from
